    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25683" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lāgus</span></b> , i, m.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the father of
				Ptolemy I. king of Egypt</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regia Lagi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					10, 527</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">famosa moenia Lagi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv. 6,
					83</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flumina Lagi, i. e. Nilus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					17, 592</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lāgēus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Lagus, Lagian</i>, <b>poet.</b> for <i>Egyptian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nilus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					1, 684</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amnis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					1, 196</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 10, 26, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ratis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					10, 322</span></i>
			.</div>
